# Hillman Minx Mk IV four-door saloon, 1945-1957.
#
# The post-war Minx range, represented by the Mk IV the pack photographs.
# The Mk I-VIII span 1945-57 and differ in trim and engine; the Mk IV is the
# best-evidenced car and the other marks are not separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hillman_Minx
#
# Dimensions 4.001 x 1.570 x 1.524 m, wheelbase 2.362 m (Mk IV).
#
# Shape reference: NO true side profile exists. Image 1 is a front
# three-quarter about 40 degrees off square; the flank is estimated from it
# and the other views within the published dimensions. The pack photographs
# a Mk IV and a Mk VII, not one car. The limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (b), a 1950 UK specification naming pastel green, dove grey
# and black. Black, Pastel Green, Dove Grey and Maroon are used. Weights 15,
# 13, 12, 10, total 50, provisional.
#
# Speed 120 km/h. Comfort 50/405, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 50. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1945 intro, retires staggered 1970-1973.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/hillman-minx-mk1-8.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/hillman-minx-mk1-8.dae. References:
# citycars/references/hillman-minx-mk1-8/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true side or rear view, so the Mk IV flank
# and tail are estimated; the boot and cabin corners are too angular. The Mk VII
# nose and larger boot were not copied, and the other marks are not separately
# represented. At 128 px the post-war three-box body and Minx grille read as a
# Minx Mk IV.


